    <statement><p>Find the absolute value of the Jacobian,
<m>\left|\frac{\partial (x,y)}{\partial (s,t)}\right|</m>,
for the change of variables given by
<m>x = 8s+2t, y = 3s+3t</m></p>
<p><m>\left|\frac{\partial(x,y)}{\partial(s,t)}\right| =</m><fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left|8\cdot 3-2\cdot 3\right|</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\frac{\partial (x,y)}{\partial (s,t)} =
  \left|\begin{array}{ccc}
     x_s \amp  x_t\\
     y_s\amp  y_t
  \end{array}\right|
  =\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
  8 \amp  2 \\
  3 \amp  3
  \end{array}\right|
  = 18.</me>
Therefore,
<me>\left|\frac{\partial (x,y)}{\partial
    (s,t)}\right|=18.</me>



</solution>
